<article class="env-lemma" id="085S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/085S">Lemma <span data-tag="085S">71.17.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X_1 \to X_2$ be a flat morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $Z_2 \subset X_2$ be a closed subspace. Let $Z_1$ be the inverse image of $Z_2$ in $X_1$. Let $X'_ i$ be the blowup of $Z_ i$ in $X_ i$. Then there exists a cartesian diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X_1' \ar[r] \ar[d] &  X_2' \ar[d] \\  X_1 \ar[r] &  X_2 }  \]
</div>
  <p> of algebraic spaces over $S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathcal{I}_2$ be the ideal sheaf of $Z_2$ in $X_2$. Denote $g : X_1 \to X_2$ the given morphism. Then the ideal sheaf $\mathcal{I}_1$ of $Z_1$ is the image of $g^*\mathcal{I}_2 \to \mathcal{O}_{X_1}$ (see Morphisms of Spaces, Definition <a href="/tag/083Q" data-tag="083Q">67.13.2</a> and discussion following the definition). By Lemma <a href="/tag/085C" data-tag="085C">71.11.5</a> we see that $X_1 \times _{X_2} X_2'$ is the relative Proj of $\bigoplus _{n \geq 0} g^*\mathcal{I}_2^ n$. Because $g$ is flat the map $g^*\mathcal{I}_2^ n \to \mathcal{O}_{X_1}$ is injective with image $\mathcal{I}_1^ n$. Thus we see that $X_1 \times _{X_2} X_2' = X_1'$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>